    ci: run every test binary in a shard (--no-fail-fast) and list every failing test
    
    The sharded core jobs ran cargo test without --no-fail-fast, so each shard
    stopped at its first failing test binary and later binaries never ran.
    The shard's --doc command was also skipped after a failure.
    
    - scripts/ci_shard.py: every test command of a shard carries --no-fail-fast.
    - scripts/ci_layer.py: a failing cargo test no longer stops the layer; the
      layer runs its remaining commands and fails at the end, and it writes
      every failing command and FAILED test to target/ci-failed-tests.md.
      The unsharded core layer gets the flag too; core-repeat no longer doubles it.
    - .github/actions/layer/action.yml: appends that summary to the job summary.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/.github/actions/layer/action.yml b/.github/actions/layer/action.yml
index 2f6318fe..6fb5d517 100644
--- a/.github/actions/layer/action.yml
+++ b/.github/actions/layer/action.yml
@@ -70,6 +70,14 @@ runs:
           --env CARGO_PROFILE_DEV_DEBUG=line-tables-only \
           mineworld-toolchain:ci python3 scripts/ci_layer.py "$LAYER" "${shard[@]}"
 
+    # Every failing test of a failed layer, listed in the job summary (scripts/ci_layer.py writes it
+    # on failure and removes any earlier copy when the layer starts). Shows nothing on a green layer.
+    - name: Summarise failing tests
+      if: always()
+      shell: bash
+      run: |
+        if [ -s target/ci-failed-tests.md ]; then cat target/ci-failed-tests.md >> "$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"; fi
+
     - name: Prune target/ before the cache is saved
       shell: bash
       run: |
